  "summary": "This experiment tested replacing ResNet50 with ViT (imagenet_vit_l) as the image encoder in a multimodal multiprofile setup with avgpool aggregation and weighted fusion, achieving 63.5% validation accuracy (vs. 63.9% for the ResNet50 baseline) and 61.8% F1. The slightly lower accuracy suggests uncertainty about ViT's relative performance compared to ResNet50 in this specific multimodal configuration, though other factors like task complexity or data characteristics may also influence the result."
}

